<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>After French Riots, Curfews &amp; Calm .. is a new Storm Brewing ? Plus Ukraine &amp; Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30e32464649791b6d987ac4af59f2e665215ff939e2f4a3408251692aa119b52</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T18:48:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261023-after-french-riots-curfews-calm-is-a-new-storm-brewing-plus-ukraine-israel" /><summary type="html">It's been a week that’s seen mass protests hijacked by violent rioters across France. The looting of shops, trashing of public buildings, the burning of Lyon’s Tourist Information and the iconic Limoges City Hall.  After the riots, came the curfews, and the contemplation, who did what and why weren’t they stopped. Seditious groups, ultra left anarchists and opportunist criminals said President Macron, with a qualified mea culpa: failures in anticipation and authorities dropped the ball in intelligence gathering. Macron is out of breath,  exhausted and disorientated claimed the Presidential Frontrunner Marine Le Pen, the far right leader now polling in an even stronger position for the Presidency. Foreign leaders had a free for all too, President Trump wading in and Israel’s prime minister settled old scores ahead of elections there. But France wasn’t isolated in its protests and unrest, Milan was a mirror image, with demonstrations in Spain, Portugal, Belgium too, An Autumn of Discontent, and more protests to follow this weekend:</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu weighs West Bank operation ahead of elections: ‘Politically, it will not help anybody’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:315717ec41c2c8e8f2f1c5e8a326e98bc55e1381b58fd7c686cf5b86f5e1dd02</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T18:26:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261023-netanyahu-weighs-west-bank-operation-ahead-of-elections-politically-it-will-not-help-anybody" /><summary type="html">As Israel approaches a consequential parliamentary election amid renewed violence in the occupied West Bank, Yedioth Ahronoth Senior Journalist Ben-Dror Yemini offers a critical assessment of Benjamin Netanyahu's political prospects, the limits of military escalation and the shifting relationship between national security and electoral legitimacy.
 
Since October 7, 2023 "Netanyahu is not popular anymore," Yemini argues, identifying the Hamas-led attacks as a decisive turning point in the Israeli prime minister's public standing.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>How Israeli settlers wearing keffiyehs are attacking West Bank olive groves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4e255bd4725b9d125da73a6fb5b611c07a3ef3c39f10b20d06a7107295c4da1</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-how-israeli-settlers-wearing-keffiyehs-are-attacking-west-bank-olive-groves" /><summary type="html">The olive harvest officially began in the West Bank on October 15, 2026, and it has coincided with an uptick in violence towards Palestinians carried out by both Israeli settlers and soldiers. Meanwhile, the settlers and soldiers have been using social media to promote an aesthetic, Instagram-friendly and nationalistic view of these harvests.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel: Could Arab parties play kingmaker in the next Knesset ?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ffc22ad45e20492fa8abcb5b9f6efd6b186821172a228f83003cafbe7963c36</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:11:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-could-arab-parties-play-kingmaker-in-the-next-knesset" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls for the first legislative election since Hamas's October 7 attacks, neither Prime Minister Benjamin #Netanyahu's Likud party nor former army chief of staff Gadi #Eisenkot's Yashar party are likely to win a majority of seats in the #Knesset. Turns out, #Israel's Arab parties could have a say in the election's outcome.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gaza : digging up the bodies from under the rubble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86e7842ac4a0455a6c8d234f116242cd457e940dcc5dd9b69f36bdb0287353c8</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:10:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261023-gaza-digging-up-the-bodies-from-under-the-rubble" /><summary type="html">One year after the ceasefire in Gaza, efforts to recover the bodies buried beneath the rubble are continuing. Civil Defense officials say 1,000 bodies have been recovered so far, but the task remains immense: between 8,000 and 10,000 more are still believed to be buried under the debris, including 3,000 in areas controlled by the Israeli army.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: France’s Macron arrives in Trappes after ‘racist terrorist attack’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c9930c5b555c81ed42587c3a466cf992eaef18176701b37005bb76c6d15a867</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:08:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261023-french-prosecutors-investigate-paris-shooting-as-suspected-terror-attack--4e9b6abddebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261023-french-prosecutors-investigate-paris-shooting-as-suspected-terror-attack" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: French student groups call for protests to continue after meeting with Macron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35f0305878b5c44a99d47e745566b76ec999eee9e6afe61ef15492c9ca37ec93</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T16:31:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261023-macron-meets-with-student-representatives-and-law-enforcement-ahead-of-new-protests--325d4c2058c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261023-macron-meets-with-student-representatives-and-law-enforcement-ahead-of-new-protests" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Extensive military operation 'on the way', Netanyahu says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21438c4932f74e850025d3fa01f516836558ac7634de6fa80630c75e339f4d67</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T15:56:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-west-bank-extensive-military-operation-on-the-way-netanyahu-says" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Friday warned of an imminent large-scale military operation in the West Bank and vowed to displace some residents of Hebron after Palestinian gunmen killed two soldiers in an attack.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yes, Israeli settlers are ripping up West Bank olive trees – but this video is fake</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e7d0b1f0ec435ef0f7aae7a7d93a75634e37202a920fdd1b3c6ccd9dd389532</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T15:56:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-yes-israeli-settlers-ripping-up-west-bank-olive-trees-%E2%80%93-but-this-video-fake" /><summary type="html">Israeli settlers and soldiers have made a habit of destroying olive trees grown by Palestinian farmers in the West Bank and, in recent days, a video showing some trees being ripped up has circulated online. Just one problem: this particular video was generated by artificial intelligence.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>AKAA art and design fair brings African artists to Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3727c96dfd88bf82715c19046a182abd7de9b76b21e76b15f954ce07a44e85fd</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T15:13:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261023-akaa-art-and-design-fair-brings-african-artists-to-paris" /><summary type="html">Every year the art and design fair AKAA, or "Also Known as Africa", brings dozens of African and Afro-descendant artists to the French capital. As the 11th edition gets underway, we welcome Nigerian painter Midegbeyan Ojisua and South African artist Olivié Keck.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Europe faces threat of organised sabotage, terrorist attacks: Estonian FM Tsahkna</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c986af721a8f325f4e7d878ac7a9f75718e5e43e20cdf6dde7715db754e2ccdb</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:55:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261023-europe-faces-threat-of-organised-sabotage-terrorist-attacks-estonian-fm-tsahkna" /><summary type="html">Estonia's counterintelligence service has recently warned that sabotage operations orchestrated by Russian special services have reached a new and dangerous phase in Europe, with targets no longer being purely symbolic. Talking Europe sits down with the country's foreign minister, Margus Tsahkna, to discuss the security situation in Estonia and the European Union in general.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU member states wrangle over all-important budget: Is a deal this year feasible?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:604de90756c09968d78177fe1c85f3a1425ca0f5308600b5cd410ef990b6c7ce</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:45:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261023-eu-member-states-wrangle-over-all-important-budget-is-a-deal-this-year-feasible" /><summary type="html">A marathon EU summit on October 15-16 failed to produce a breakthrough on the European Union's next long-term budget. Although EU leaders put on a brave face at the end of the talks by saying that "the way forward is clearer", EU capitals appear deadlocked on what that path is. At stake is the EU's ability to finance its strategic priorities from 2028 to 2034. The main dividing line is between the so-called "frugal countries", who want deep cuts to the proposed budget, and the "friends of cohesion", who say that cuts are not the answer.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Deadly shooting west of Paris ‘clearly terrorist’ attack, French interior minister says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a16021096bac0a98a62476ecbccaf3cdeb7c52bec4b9698fa1434ce11c5ffc01</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:43:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261023-french-prosecutors-investigate-paris-shooting-as-suspected-terror-attack--4e9b6abddebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261023-french-prosecutors-investigate-paris-shooting-as-suspected-terror-attack" /></entry><entry><title>‘I killed lots of terrorists, but it didn’t make me feel better’: The trauma haunting Israel's elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e724d34f205afe3f57f7b26a469a43cfe84fdf8a2ee4416f2262c0b749c238cf</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:32:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-i-killed-lots-of-terrorists-but-it-didn-t-make-me-feel-better-the-trauma-haunting-israel-s-elections" /><summary type="html">After more than three years of war, the number of Israeli soldiers suffering from post-traumatic stress disorder following bloody campaigns in Gaza and Lebanon has risen drastically. In the lead-up to Israel’s crucial legislative elections, FRANCE 24 speaks with soldiers left shell-shocked by the country’s wars.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>French protests: President Emmanuel Macron meets student unions representatives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f87029fa5b39e187a75028d197c24eafee2d16848838c9bacf762e377ca5003</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:26:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-protests-president-emmanuel-macron-meets-student-unions-representatives" /><summary type="html">For the first time since the beginning of the mobilisation, French President Emmanuel Macron is set to meet student representatives as the government prepares for tomorrow's mobilisation. Luke Shrago has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Suspect arrested after 1 killed and 4 wounded in a shooting in Paris suburb</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e95ffd2972f099498c8a1252217df014ec0a7950760754defab915556c6982a3</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:24:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/suspect-arrested-after-1-killed-and-4-wounded-in-a-shooting-in-paris-suburb" /><summary type="html">A gunman firing from a vehicle in a Paris suburb Friday killed one person and wounded several others, including a 12-year-old girl, in what French authorities suspect may have been a racially motivated attack.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Gunman kills one and wounds four in town outside Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ee1b403a7eee327e982a30c3a5675b1aaa8ee5ab4c84236e70748b7b7e143a6</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:21:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-gunman-kills-one-and-wounds-four-in-town-outside-paris" /><summary type="html">Eliza Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Several killed, dozens wounded in Jordan church shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca9b92d43b92c876321ff306c3405bd66b0064ed72737e7343acca37e5c71082</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:16:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-several-killed-dozens-wounded-in-jordan-church-shooting" /><summary type="html">At least seven people have been killed and 34 others wounded in a church shooting in Jordan, authorities said Friday. The unidentified assailants allegedly attacked the Greek Orthodox church during a funeral in the Karak directorate in the central part of the country.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Why do women in public life become targets?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c222ccb3a2046afcd8c85280e811c648d1f18dbb975b201aa8baecabd0e8fbc5</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T13:58:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261023-why-do-women-in-public-life-become-targets" /><summary type="html">A brutal targeted attack on an Australian female MP, who lost both her legs as a result, has reignited concerns over the rising levels of violence against women in public life. Also Cornell University is facing a no-confidence vote over its handling of an alleged gang rape in 2024. Annette Young speaks to Annie E. Clark, a survivor of campus sexual assault and Dr Sara Wilf of George Mason University about why institutions continue to struggle with sexual assault cases.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>French authorities tighten restrictions and ban specific protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:effad463b0ba717f3c36bb44c00d6da0b134f5003e057c68d68ced0e3a39fc99</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T13:55:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-french-authorities-tighten-restrictions-and-ban-specific-protests-1" /><summary type="html">France is bracing for another weekend of protests, after violence erupted on the sidelines of last week's mobilisations. Paris is extending a partial curfew in parts of the city until Monday, while protests are banned altogether in the cities of Marseille and Lyon. 70,000 security personnel will be deployed on Saturday and only union demonstrations will be authorised.</summary></entry><entry><title>Major protests in France: "There is a frustration that has accumulated"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:229a34415272cef3719eed7c9581e9333033ab5baeac2c0617569b155caa05b3</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T13:20:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/major-protests-in-france-macron-convenes-student-representatives--222e3ff88ce4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/major-protests-in-france-macron-convenes-student-representatives" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is set to meet with high school pupils whose protests over school conditions have sparked a broader movement. Details by Philippe Moreau-Chevrolet, communication specialist and teacher at Sciences Po.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Spiralling situation': Political paralysis deepening France's socioeconomic crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4bcf11f62818a185f2d7c1e5d6e0db92ce6f04b9289e0d328453ca8c6641591e</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T13:10:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-awaits-moody-s-verdict-downgrade-widely-expected-as-debt-fears-grow--ef94e5636e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-awaits-moody-s-verdict-downgrade-widely-expected-as-debt-fears-grow" /><summary type="html">France's deepening fiscal crisis is testing the sustainability of current sociopolitical and economic policy. For Oliver Davies, Professor and Head of the Department of French at University College Cork, the crisis is not simply the consequence of deteriorating public finances. It is also the product of President Emmanuel Macron's political choices, particularly his decision to dissolve the National Assembly in June 2024. Davies describes the resulting parliamentary deadlock as a "self-inflicted crisis", warning that the market confidence on which Macron has long relied "now seems to be evaporating."</summary></entry><entry><title>War in the Middle East: Israel launches West Bank operations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93d5c248b58aa7ed8e7cfa37f75a8b45e7bac1a23eef54fc1be008f2c279975f</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:57:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/war-in-the-middle-east-israel-launches-west-bank-operations--85a7b4908438.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/war-in-the-middle-east-israel-launches-west-bank-operations" /><summary type="html">Palestinian militants wounded five Israelis in an attack on Friday before being killed in a shootout with soldiers, leading Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu to order a lockdown in the occupied West Bank days before Israeli elections. Details by Kethevane Gorjestani, FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil's tense presidential run-off campaign feels like a psychological thriller</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:410ec813ff0229f3fe32adce8d02f19602fc24a03bb2d941baac8efb4851fa05</id><updated>2026-10-23T19:59:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:45:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-brazil-s-tense-presidential-run-off-campaign-feels-like-a-psychological-thriller--934b659fa2c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-brazil-s-tense-presidential-run-off-campaign-feels-like-a-psychological-thriller" /><summary type="html">Insults traded on social media and a combative debate have intensified the pressure ahead of a fiercely contested presidential run-off on Sunday, with only a few points separating leftist pro-union President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and far-right challenger Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of former president and Trump ally Jair Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
